note S5 dit (OMEGESE 9.13.1): `dit v` sets PSTATE.DIT from v and gives the previous bit. Linux starts a
note process with DIT 0. Exit 0 when the sequence 0 -> 1 -> 0 reads back as expected, else the check's number.
om2
fn main to int
a = dit 0
if ne a 0
ret 1
end
b = dit 1
if ne b 0
ret 2
end
c = dit 0
if ne c 1
ret 3
end
d = dit 0
if ne d 0
ret 4
end
v = int 1
e = dit v
f = dit sub v 1
if ne add e f 1
ret 5
end
g = add dit 1 dit 1
if ne g 1
ret 6
end
h = dit 0
if ne h 1
ret 7
end
ret 0
end
